_irNotes: {
	"decision-durability": "Durability: the game is tab, the records device. A game in progress lives as long as the tab, as it did in the original's window; only Best Times was ever kept, and here it survives a reload in this browser. Levels are three routes rather than a resize of one field: each level keeps its own rows and its own game, the field is seeded by CUE for all three, and no reduce ever has to add or remove squares"
	"decision-escape-hatches": "Escape hatches: none. No container, WASM unit, vendored component or external endpoint; every line of app code is a handler the terminal runs in a compartment"
	"decision-guests": "Sign-in: guests, minted silently. The brief asked for Google sign-in through Firebase. The terminal offers passkey and guest and nothing else (Firebase is its planned third mode), and pronto refuses a program that demands a mode the terminal lacks. The edge tier, where this app is released, signs in guests only: passkeys need the auth service's ceremonies, which the edge does not run. So auth.required is false, the terminal mints a guest at boot, and a guest's session lives as long as the tab. A winner types a name with each post, as the original's record box asked for one"
	"decision-hosting": "Released to Cloudflare, not Pages. A ranking every player shares needs a cluster every player reaches. The Pages target runs a whole cluster inside each tab, so its Hall of Fame would hold one player's wins. The edge target runs one cluster in a Durable Object behind a Worker, and serves guests"
	"decision-score-writes": "Score: everyone reads, the owner inserts. #Access has no such mode, so Score is declared public and 011_score_writes.sql adds one permissive INSERT arm, WITH CHECK (user_id = auth_uid()), as realworld's owner writes do. There is no UPDATE and no DELETE arm. Declaring it private and widening SELECT in SQL would make the browser believe \"mine\" where the server means \"everyone's\""
}

